The code-level pushforward of the code-level pullback of an element of the second system is that element.

By extensionality of elements it is enough to compare membership of an arbitrary neighbourhood. If the neighbourhood is the basic neighbourhood of an X-sequence code m whose index neighbourhood equals the basic neighbourhood of a Y-sequence code n met by the element, the cross-parity equality identifies the X-sequence neighbourhood with the basic neighbourhood of n, which the element meets. Conversely, if the element meets the neighbourhood, surjectivity names it as a basic neighbourhood of some index n, and the reverse of the same equality at the Y-sequence code of n and n supplies the X-sequence witness, with the remaining equations holding by reflexivity.
